==English==
[[File:Newone - TMG thickness gauge. Thước đo độ dày.jpg|thumb|Thickness gauge]]
[[File:Pick thickness.jpg|thumb|Measuring the '''thickness''' of a guitar [[pick]] with [[calipers]]. The measured thickness is 2.0 mm.]]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|thikkenesse}}, {{m|enm|thiknesse}}, from {{inh|en|ang|þicnes|t=thickness, viscosity, density, hardness; obscurity, cloud, darkness; thicket; depth, a thick body, anything thick or heavy}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*þikkwīnassī|t=thickness}}, equivalent to {{suf|en|thick|ness}}. Cognate with {{cog|fy|tsjokkens|t=thickness}}, {{cog|goh|dickinessī}}, {{m|goh|dikkinissi}}, {{m|goh|diknissi|t=thickness, density}}. Eclipsed non-native {{noncog|enm|crassitude|t=thickness}}  from {{noncog|la|crassitūdō|t=thickness}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈθɪknəs/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪknəs|s=2}}
* {{hyph|en|thick|ness}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The property of being [[thick]] (in dimension).
# {{lb|en|uncountable|countable}} A measure of how thick (in dimension) something is.
#: {{ux|en|The '''thickness''' of the Earth's crust varies from two to 70 kilometres.}}
#: {{ux|en|Guitar picks come in different '''thicknesses'''.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A layer.
#: {{ux|en|We upholstered the seat with three '''thicknesses''' of cloth to make it more comfortable to sit on.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The quality of being thick (in consistency).
#: {{ux|en|Whip the cream until it reaches a good '''thickness'''.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable|informal}} The property of being thick (slow to understand).
# {{lb|en|graph theory|countable}} The [[minimum]] number of [[planar]] [[subgraph]]s which a given graph can [[decompose]] into.

